    "title": {
     "en": "Change from the shopkeeper"
    },
    "text": {
     "en": "Reena bought groceries for ₹209. She gave a ₹500 note to Peter uncle. How much should he return?"
    }
   },
   {
    "id": "explain",
    "type": "explanation",
    "provenance": "original",
    "keepEnglishTerms": [
     "bill",
     "change",
     "subtract",
     "balance"
    ],
    "text": {
     "en": "Peter uncle runs a shop. Reena bought groceries for ₹209 and gave a ₹500 note.\nThe money returned is called change. To find change subtract the bill from the money given.\n500 - 209 = 291. Peter uncle returns ₹291.\nCheck by adding: 209 + 291 = 500.\nAnother way: count up from 209 to 300 which is 91, then to 500 which is 200 more, so 291.\nAlways draw the problem before solving. Avoid looking for keywords only."
    }
   },
